we are extremely excited about our new  program in bilingual education  this is one of the few programs where  you can get a license in bilingual  education in nevada  so again we are extremely excited about  this  in a district where we have over 40  percent latino latinx  and a large majority of spanish speakers  in this valley  it's extremely important for people to  understand the power  of speaking two languages and also the  power that it provides for our children  in the valley who are english learners  and who are bilingual to have teachers  who are prepared  to use their language to support their  needs in the classroom  if you are a speaker of two languages  this is power  sometimes in the united states we hear  that there is no power in being  bilingual but having a program like this  really demonstrates the power also it  shows the academics  the way that you can excel academically  when you are able to use both languages  in the classroom  we have a lot of people who are spanish  speakers who might speak spanish  socially  but might not have the academic language  that they need and so this allows our  children to be able to  have that academic language that they  use in school in english and in spanish  our goal is to enroll 30 students by the  fall of 2021 into this program  so we're we're in in process of that  right now  we want to make sure that students are  provided an opportunity to actually get  out there in the community  and see the power of this tool in the  community and i think that's one of the  most important pieces  is the children the sooner we can get  students out there with children  the better and so that's one of the  things that we'll focus on in this  program  is bringing students in and constantly  examining the program and how well we're  doing and  what areas that we need to change our  focus is i mean transition or the types  of bilingual program models that exist  are part of the district so  our goal is to prepare teachers to  potentially be in what will be known as  a dual language bilingual classroom  in other words half of the day would be  in english and half of the day would be  in spanish  so our students will be prepared for  whatever program model that is  being used at the school whether it's  transitional or dual language  we do have two pathways we have a  heritage spanish speaker pathway  for students who may have been raised  speaking spanish and who just want to  improve their their spanish and english  and then we also have a  non-heritage pathway for students like  myself who may have learned spanish as a  second language  so is this degree is this the first  degree of its kind in  nevada or southern nevada we had this  program many years ago  and it was inactive for many years and  with our hsi grant we were able to  revive the program  everything we do in the school of ed is  a partnership with ccsd and i say that  because we have to place our students  into classrooms for student teaching  experiences and they're usually in ccsd  although we do have some that are with  private schools or charter schools as  well but yes  that's the foundation of everything we  do our partnerships the foundation of  our program is social justice  so our students are trained to work with  families and to allow students to  celebrate their families and their  culture when they come into the class if  you're interested in enrolling in our  program  feel free to contact us at 702  or you can email us at nsc.edu
 

